# Files that must never be served as public static assets.
#
# Vercel uploads every tracked file and serves it at its path, so before this
# existed https://admin.threepin.in/docs/SOP.md returned 200 to anyone. The
# runtime needs none of the below: api/*.js imports only from api/ and from
# crm-assets/dashboardMetrics.js, and every scripts/ reference in api/ is a
# comment, not an import.
#
# docs/api.html is deliberately NOT excluded — it is the public partner-facing
# API reference. Only the internal markdown in that folder is blocked.

docs/*.md
User manual/
backups/
scripts/
*.tsv

# The security rules are enforced server-side, but publishing them hands an
# attacker the whole tenancy model for free.
firestore.rules

# Internal repo readme, not a site page.
README.md

# Belt-and-braces: also covered by .gitignore, so this only matters for a
# `vercel deploy` run from a working tree that has one lying around.
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
.env*

# Internal to the finance build — the reference prototype, the build kit and the test
# suite are working material, not part of the deployed site. Without these they would be
# served as static files at their own URLs.
reference/
FINANCE/
tests/
storage.rules
